From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: McKack <4465550+McKack@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 20:01:40 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] d3d12: occlusion and timestamp queries

Occlusion queries count samples through Metal visibility results: draws go into a new 64-bit slot whenever the set of running queries changes or a render pass starts, and a compute pass sums each ended query's slots into its heap. Binary results are made 0/1 when resolved. Timestamp queries sample Metal's GPU timestamp counters at the end of an empty blit pass.
